# LCD fixed-width overlay rendering

The Master UI draws on a **16×2** character LCD. Screens are **not cleared** on each refresh; new values are printed over the previous ones at fixed cursor positions. This is intentional and cheaper than `lcd.clear()` / full redraws.

## Rules when changing Menu / Draw text

1. **Same field → same character count** as whatever can appear in that slot (including spaces). A shorter string leaves **ghost characters** from the previous value.
2. Prefer padding with trailing spaces over clearing the line.
3. Full-line messages should be **exactly 16 characters** (or print spaces to the end of the line).
4. Info time WORK/WAIT durations use **5 characters**, matching `formatMsToTime()` (`dtostrf` width 4 + unit). Alternatives in that slot:
   - `hold ` — schedule ready / tank full / pump held off
   - `[\xF3]  ` — wait longer than `MaxDaysInMillis` (pad to 5)
5. Do not introduce variable-length status phrases (`"Held off"`, `"Waiting…"`) into a fixed slot unless the whole line layout is redesigned around them.

## Example

```cpp
// BAD — "off" is 3 chars; previous "12.5m" leaves trailing "m"
lcd.print(F("off"));

// GOOD — same width as formatMsToTime
lcd.print(F("hold "));
```
